==Danish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/spoːrə/|[ˈsb̥oːɐ]|lang=da}}

===Etymology 1===
* {{sense|spore}}, from {{etyl|grc|da}} {{term|σπορά|lang=grc|sc=polytonic|tr=spora||seed, a sowing}}.
* {{sense|spur}}, from {{etyl|non|da}} {{term|spori|lang=non}}.

====Noun====
{{da-noun|n|r}}

# [[spore#English|spore]] {{gloss|reproductive particle}}
# [[spore#English|spore]] {{gloss|resistant particle produced by bacterium or protist}}
# [[spur]] {{gloss|a rigid implement, often roughly y-shaped, that is fixed to one's heel for purpose of prodding a horse}}
# [[spur]] {{gloss|anything that inspires or motivates, as a spur does to a horse}}
# [[spur]] {{gloss|an appendage or spike pointing rearward, near the foot, for instance that of a rooster}}

=====Inflection=====
{{da-noun-infl|n|r}}

===Etymology 2===
* {{sense|to spur}}, from {{term|spore||spur|lang=da}}.
* {{sense|to trace}}, from {{term|spor||track, trail, scent|lang=da}}.

====Verb====
{{da-verb|spor|spore|sporer|sporede|er/har|sporet}}

# [[spur]] {{gloss|to prod}}
# [[spur]] {{gloss|to urge or encourage to action, or to a more vigorous pursuit of an object; to incite; to stimulate; to instigate; to impel; to drive}}
# [[trace]] {{gloss|to follow the trail of}}
# [[scent]] {{gloss|to detect the scent of}}
# [[feel]], [[notice]], [[perceive]]

